WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160
JAMES ANDERSON:
Revolutionary developments

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.680
in the union of chemistry
and physics hold

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.230
the key to solving
unprecedented global problems.

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:12.420
But understanding the central role
that chemistry and technical forces

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:16.020
play in addressing these
problems requires learning

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:18.390
the fundamental scientific concepts.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.570
Join me to learn the
foundations of chemistry,

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:25.770
ranging from molecular structures
and thermodynamics, to entropy,

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:30.900
and equilibria to electrochemistry and
how to apply these scientific concepts

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.189
to our modern world.

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:34.680
Throughout each course,
you will not only

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:38.790
gain quantitative reasoning
and critical thinking skills,

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:42.420
but also, will be able to
directly link scientific concepts

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:45.630
to current global strategies
on energy production

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:51.030
and use in the context of rapid changes
in the Earth's climate structure.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:54.690
These courses can be taken
together for college credit

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:58.170
through edX's MicroBachelors programs.

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:02.220
Learn chemistry while earning
college credit for your future.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:04.019
Chemistry can change the world.

00:01:04.019 --> 00:01:07.009
Are you ready to shape the future?

